# Ghostty Theme: Aura Light
#
# Aura is a dark theme and publishes no light edition, so this is derived. The derivation is
# arithmetic and can be rerun, and it was rerun once after the first attempt was measured
# against real light themes and found wanting.
#
# Inverting does not work. Aura's accents sit high in lightness, which is what makes them
# glow on a near black page, and the mint #61ffca against white is about 1.3 to 1. What
# carries identity across the switch is hue, so every accent keeps its hue angle and only
# lightness and chroma move. The page keeps the dark background's own hue too, so it is a
# faint lavender white rather than a neutral one.
#
# The work is done in OKLCh rather than CIELAB. Lab's hue lines bend under a lightness
# change, most visibly with blue drifting toward purple, and this derivation changes
# lightness by a lot.
#
# The first attempt solved each accent independently against a flat 4.5 to 1 target, which
# made the target the design. It produced a contrast spread of 1.11x where Aura Dark's own
# accents span 2.52x, so the theme's internal hierarchy was flattened out of existence.
# Measuring three shipped light themes settled it, Catppuccin Latte spans 2.07x, GitHub
# Light Default 2.52x and Rose Pine Dawn 2.73x. Flat was the outlier, not the norm.
#
# So each accent's contrast against the dark page is measured, and it is placed at the
# lightness reproducing its rank against this page, over a band compressed to 1.73x because
# sRGB holds less chroma at low lightness than at high. Chroma comes from the dark theme's
# own chroma, not from the gamut maximum at each hue, which is what the first attempt used
# and why it amplified the loud accents and muted the quiet ones.
#
# Green, orange and blue clamp against the gamut on the way down. Orange is the worst of it,
# since a dark orange is a brown and there is no way around that, which is the same wall
# every light theme meets.
#
# Slot 0 is the ink and slots 7 and 15 are light greys, the light theme convention. The
# #949494 rule from 9424044 is a value for a dark page and does not apply, so the comment
# grey is solved the same way as the accents.

# Set the background and foreground colors
background = #f8f7fb
foreground = #474556

# Set the cursor color
cursor-color = #7e54d1
cursor-text = #f8f7fb

# Set the selection colors
selection-background = #dfdaf2
selection-foreground = #474556

# Define the color palette
palette = 0=#474556
palette = 1=#bf3239
palette = 2=#00805f
palette = 3=#6b4400
palette = 4=#7e54d1
palette = 5=#872f90
